 833:source\asw/mp3.c **** /**
 834:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * \brief Read one block of PCM, convert it and fill the inactive sound buffer.
 835:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *
 836:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * The DBG pins show the time of the three steps on the oscilloscope:
 837:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * DBG_FS = FS_Read(), DBG_CONV = conversion, DBG_FILL = SOUND_FillBuffer(),
 838:source\asw/mp3.c ****  * DBG_DEAD = from the buffer swap in the ISR until this function is done.
 839:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *
 840:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *   Format         block_align  raw bytes per 1024 output samples
 841:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *   8-bit  mono         1          1024   (no conversion)
 842:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *   16-bit mono         2          2048
 843:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *   24-bit mono         3          3072
 844:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *   stereo           2 x mono   2 x mono   (L+R averaged, N3)
 845:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *   44100 Hz           2 x      (2 frames averaged, N4)
 846:source\asw/mp3.c ****  *
